body:
**Describe the bug**
I'm upgrading form 1.2.0.Final to 1.3.0.Final and my Tests stopped working when  implementing  `inject` method from `QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager`

I'm injecting AMQ client session in very similar way like in  https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/test-framework/kubernetes-client/src/main/java/io/quarkus/test/kubernetes/client/KubernetesMockServerTestResource.java 

My implementation
```
    @Override
    public void inject(Object testInstance) {
        log.info("Inject client session to test");

        Class<?> c = testInstance.getClass();
        while (c != Object.class) {
            for (Field f : c.getDeclaredFields()) {
                if (f.getAnnotation(JMSClientSession.class) != null) {
                    if (!javax.jms.Session.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())) {
                        throw new RuntimeException("@JMSClientSession can only be used on fields of type javax.jms.Session");
                    }

                    f.setAccessible(true);
                    try {
                        f.set(testInstance, session);
                        return;
                    } catch (Exception e) {
                        throw new RuntimeException(e);
                    }
                }
            }
            c = c.getSuperclass();
        }
    }
```

**Expected behavior**
Client session is injected

**Actual behavior**
f.getAnnotation(JMSClientSession.class) returns always null.
Then My Test case fails on NPE because field session is null

**To Reproduce**
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1. Try to run Test that would inject  into field something in similar way like in  https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/test-framework/kubernetes-client/src/main/java/io/quarkus/test/kubernetes/client/KubernetesMockServerTestResource.java and in test use the injected value.

